Vulkan: a sampler a program declares but a draw sets no texture for. OpenGL samples such a sampler as black and
the engine's draws rely on it (a fixed-function program declares five texture stages and a draw binds the ones
the material uses; a stage without a texture is never sampled). bgfx's Vulkan backend left the descriptor of such
a sampler unwritten, which Vulkan does not allow for a descriptor the pipeline uses statically (lavapipe crashes in
the shader, other drivers read whatever the pool held). The host now gives bgfx one texture per kind (2D, cube,
3D; bgfx::setVkUnboundTextures, the engine: src/shim/context.cpp) and an unset sampler gets the one of its kind.
The kinds a program declares are part of the descriptor set's cache key.

